   {
    "id": "p_00006",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The [I5]free[/I5]() function shall cause the space pointed to by [I6]ptr[/I6] to be deallocated; that is, made available for further\nallocation. If [I7]ptr[/I7] is a null pointer, no action shall occur. Otherwise, if the argument does not match a pointer earlier\nreturned by [A8][I9]aligned_alloc[/I9]()[/A8], [A10][I11]calloc[/I11]()[/A10], [A12][I13]malloc[/I13]()[/A12],\n\n[S14][[A15]ADV[/A15]][/S14] [IMG16]\n[A17][I18]posix_memalign[/I18]()[/A17], [IMG19] [A20][I21]realloc[/I21]()[/A20],\n\n[S22][[A23]CX[/A23]][/S22] [IMG24]\n[A25][I26]reallocarray[/I26]()[/A25], or a function in POSIX.1-2024 that allocates memory as if by\n[A27][I28]malloc[/I28]()[/A27], [IMG29] or if the\nspace has been deallocated by a call to [I30]free[/I30](), [S31][[A32]CX[/A32]][/S31] [IMG33] [A34][I35]reallocarray[/I35]()[/A34],\n[IMG36] or [A37][I38]realloc[/I38]()[/A37], the\nbehavior is undefined.",
    "placeholders": {
