   {
    "id": "p_00009",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     9
    ],
    "text": "For purposes of determining the existence of a data race, [I48]free[/I48]() shall behave as though it accessed only memory locations\naccessible through its argument and not other static duration storage. The function may, however, visibly modify the storage that\nit deallocates. Calls to [A49][I50]aligned_alloc[/I50]()[/A49], [A51][I52]calloc[/I52]()[/A51], [I53]free[/I53](), [A54][I55]malloc[/I55]()[/A54],\n[S56][[A57]ADV[/A57]][/S56] [IMG58]\n[A59][I60]posix_memalign[/I60]()[/A59], [IMG61]\n\n[S62][[A63]CX[/A63]][/S62] [IMG64]\n[A65][I66]reallocarray[/I66]()[/A65], [IMG67]\nand [A68][I69]realloc[/I69]()[/A68] that allocate or deallocate a particular region of memory shall occur\nin a single total order (see XBD [A70][I71]4.15.1 Memory Ordering[/I71][/A70]), and each\nsuch deallocation call shall synchronize with the next allocation (if any) in this order.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I48": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
